  "penalties": [],
  "extra_findings": [
    "SEC-017/SEC-016 variant (listing/search) — any logged-in client sees every client's tickets in the list and search, index.php:72-73 / lib.php:80-85 (F3; fixed via listarChamadosDoDono)",
    "SEC-017/SEC-016 variant (export) — ?export=csv returns every ticket to any logged-in client, index.php:44-46 / lib.php:132 (F4; fixed by filtering the web export to the session owner, exportarCsv() kept unfiltered)",
    "BUG-011 — exportarCsv writes to a fixed shared EXPORT_DIR/chamados.csv and readfile()s it; concurrent exports corrupt each other (NUL holes, truncation), lib.php:125-150 (F9; fixed with an in-memory buffer and atomic copy)",
    "SEC-020 — persistent copy of all tickets at a predictable path in EXPORT_DIR, fopen('w') follows symlinks, lib.php:125-126 (F15; mitigated only)",
    "Session cookie without HttpOnly/SameSite/Secure, index.php:15 (F14; fixed)",
    "SEC-019 — no login attempt limiting, index.php:20-29 (F16; reported only)",
    "PERF-003 — listing and CSV unpaginated, memory blow-up on large tables, lib.php:80-85 (F17; reported only)",
    "PERF-002 — SELECT * pulls the TEXT descricao column the listing never shows, lib.php:80/132 (F17, decision 6; CSV query narrowed)",
    "PERF-009 — mediaResposta fetches every row to sum in PHP, lib.php:109-115 (F18; replaced by SUM/COUNT)",
    "PERF-015 — PHP session lock held for the whole request, index.php:15-39 (F19; session_write_close added)",
    "Array-shaped POST/GET parameters raise TypeError (HTTP 500), index.php:22 and :72-73 (F20; fixed)",
    "Connection-failure check is dead code on PHP 8.1+ and display_errors could leak details, index.php:9-13 (F21; fixed)",
    "fputcsv() called without $escape, deprecated on PHP 8.4, lib.php:130/138 (F22; explicit default passed)",
    "Role cached in the session is never revalidated, index.php:38-39 (F23; reported only)",
    "No logout route or explicit session lifetime, index.php:15 (F24; reported only)",
    "formatarStatus maps any unknown status to 'Resolvido', lib.php:32-34 (F26; reported only, behaviour deliberately kept)",
    "Critical unanswered ticket is never flagged as SLA breached, lib.php:56-58 (F27; low-confidence business-rule hypothesis, reported only)",
    "LIKE wildcards % and _ not escaped in the search term, lib.php:82 (F28; deliberately left; part of a complete SEC-001 fix per the matrix note)",
    "Hardening — tecnicoNome()/verChamado() concatenate int-typed ids into SQL, lib.php:69/100; correctly stated as not exploitable today (F29; switched to prepared statements)",
    "SEC-005 — no CSRF token on the login POST, index.php:32 (named in decision 10 of section 3; not changed)"
  ],
